<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">García Sánchez III of Pamplona</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1012–<a href="/years/1054">1054</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as García of Nájera</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">García Sánchez III (c. 1012–1054) was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pamplona">Pamplona</a> from 1035, the eldest legitimate son of Sancho III the Great. He ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/najera">Nájera</a>, where he founded the monastery of Santa María la Real, and took part in campaigns against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taifa">taifa</a> kingdoms. Rivalry with his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-i-of-leon">Ferdinand I of León</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> ended in war, and he was killed at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-atapuerca">Battle of Atapuerca</a> in 1054.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/garcia-sanchez-iii-of-pamplona.jpg" alt="García Sánchez III of Pamplona" width="295" height="568" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Garcia_(III)_Sanches_de_Navarra_-_Compendio_de_cr%C3%B3nicas_de_reyes_(Biblioteca_Nacional_de_Espa%C3%B1a).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
